{"id":"2c6d48e2-e133-453e-9223-cf6874012a76","object":"chat.completion","created":1784997566,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    names = [seg['name'] for seg in segments]\\n    importances = [seg['importance'] for seg in segments]\\n    minima = [seg['minimum'] for seg in segments]\\n    capacities = [seg['capacity'] for seg in segments]\\n\\n    sum_min = sum(minima)\\n    sum_cap = sum(capacities)\\n\\n    if sum_min > budget:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"Budget {budget} less than sum of minima {sum_min}\\\")\\n    if budget > sum_cap:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"Budget {budget} exceeds total capacity {sum_cap}\\\")\\n\\n    allocations = list(minima)\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        # compute best segment among those not at capacity\\n        best_i = -1\\n        best_ratio = -1.0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if allocations[i] < capacities[i]:\\n                ratio = importances[i] / (allocations[i] + 1)\\n                if ratio > best_ratio or (ratio == best_ratio and (best_i == -1 or i < best_i)):\\n                    best_ratio = ratio\\n                    best_i = i\\n        if best_i == -1:\\n            # shouldn't happen because budget <= total capacity\\n            break\\n        allocations[best_i] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n\\n    by_name = {names[i]: allocations[i] for i in range(n)}\\n    total = sum(allocations)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"allocations\\\": allocations,\\n        \\\"by_name\\\": by_name,\\n        \\\"total\\\": total\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) function per the specification. The case has a payload with segments and budget. We need to allocate budget to segments: each segment has name, importance, minimum, capacity. We give each segment its minimum first, then distribute remaining budget (if any) one token at a time, each time picking the segment with highest importance / next_allocated_position (i.e., current allocated+1), with ties broken by original segment order (index). Need to return allocations (list of integers in same order as segments?), by_name (dict mapping segment name to its allocation), total (sum of allocations). The output schema says allocations is array of integers, by_name is object with dynamic keys from case.segments[*].name, each integer. total integer.\n\nWe must handle invalid: if sum of minimum exceeds budget, or if budget exceeds total capacity (sum of capacities). Raise ValueError.\n\nImplementation: Parse case, extract segments list, budget. Create lists of names, importances, minima, capacities. Compute sum_min, sum_cap. Check. Initialize allocations = list of minima. Remaining = budget - sum_min. While remaining > 0: For each segment, compute \"value\" = importance / (allocations[i] + 1) (since next position is current+1). Actually the description: \"give one token to the segment maximizing importance divided by its next allocated position.\" The next allocated position is the slot after current allocation? If we add one token, the new total would be current+1. The ratio should be importance / (current_alloc+1)? Because the next position is the one we are about to assign. That makes sense. So compute ratio = importance / (allocations[i] + 1). Pick max ratio, tie break by original order (i index). Increase allocations[i] by 1, remaining--. Also check capacity: we must not exceed capacity. So before adding, we need to ensure we don't exceed capacity. If a segment already at capacity, skip it (or ratio should be -inf). So we only consider segments with current allocation < capacity. If no segment available (budget left but all at capacity), then remaining budget cannot be allocated, but budget might be allowed? The spec says \"Reject budgets below the quota sum or above total capacity.\" So budget <= total capacity. So if leftover but all at capacity, that would mean budget == total capacity, so no leftover. Good.\n\nAfter loop, compute total = sum(allocations). Build by_name dict. Return dict with keys: allocations, by_name, total.\n\nNote: the case payload may have other fields like _case_nonce; we ignore them.\n\nTesting with given fixtures: they all seem feasible.\n\nEdge cases: floating point division? Use float. For tie break, we can compare tuples (ratio, -index) because higher ratio first, and if equal, lower index. We'll pick max using max() with key.\n\nNow produce JSON output with implementation key containing Python source string. Must escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nWrite code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1496,"completion_tokens":1048,"total_tokens":2544,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":634},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":88},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}